{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"f measure for classification f measure for classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","fileName":"F-Measure for Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"F-Measure for Classification","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-14 21:00\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Classification Evaluation and Visualization]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Evaluation and Visualization","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"f measure for classification f measure for classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","fileName":"F-Measure for Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"F-Measure for Classification","heading":"F-Measure for Classification","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The F-measure for classification is the harmonic mean of precision and recall. The F1 score weights them equally, while the more general F-beta score places greater emphasis on recall when beta is above one and on precision when it is below one.\n\nBecause both components depend on the chosen positive class and decision threshold, the score should be interpreted with the application's error costs and class distribution in view.\n\nThe book calculates the measure from held-out confusion-matrix counts so a model must balance successful positive retrieval against the reliability of positive predictions. The appropriate balance remains dependent on the costs of false positives and false negatives.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Evaluation and Visualization","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"f measure for classification f measure for classification","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/F-Measure for Classification.md","fileName":"F-Measure for Classification.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"F-Measure for Classification","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[dataclassification.pdf]]\n\n[[essentialsofdatascience.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Classification Evaluation and Visualization","dataclassification.pdf","essentialsofdatascience.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}